 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "FROM HER ROBING-SHIP - REV. JONAS John\nTo him in long balm, which gave relief,\nA soul to health, and a breast within\nWhereof the soul was blest; but his vision\nWas lost by fire; he never knew\nThe loveliness of her wither'd forehead,\nNor the soft pallor of her drowsy eyes.\nHe had been blind without this surprise,\nBut when he saw the wan pitiless face,\nIts evil eye burning through again,\nAnd heard her voice, at an untimely hour,\nHer weary words, now aye unanswer'd: then",
